---
description: >
  Brevity-sweep audit of `src/tools/upgrade/.aide` — 13 desired outcomes (cap 4), 8 undesired; description and intent close to caps but body Strategy and outcomes carry the entire ten-category enumeration verbatim.
intent: >
  aide_upgrade is the agent-driven interactive upgrade tool. Spec is bloated
  by enumerating each of the ten categories by name across both outcomes and
  Strategy, plus a long MCP-tool-description meta-outcome that restates the
  contract surface byte-for-byte.
misalignment:
  - spec-bloat
---

## Issues

- [ ] `description` is 156 chars (under cap, fine).

- [ ] `intent` is 166 words (over cap 100). Trim the prescription-pattern
  paragraph and the malformed-JSON aside.
  Traces to: `intent` field | Brevity Contract caps
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity

- [ ] `outcomes.desired` has 13 items (cap 4); most enumerate one slice of
  the contract (per-file results, per-category control, MCP merge as
  prescription, malformed JSON reporting, agent-not-tool writes
  methodology files, brain category detection-only with three-value vocabulary,
  MCP-tool-description meta-outcome enumerating all ten category names).
  Compress to 3-4 falsifiable domain criteria.
  Traces to: `outcomes.desired` | Brevity Contract caps + Forbidden content (category-name enumeration, function names)
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Forbidden-content

- [ ] `outcomes.undesired` has 11 paragraph-length items including a meta-rule
  about MCP-description-drift that re-enumerates the ten category names.
  Compress.
  Traces to: `outcomes.undesired` | Brevity Contract caps + Forbidden content
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Forbidden-content

- [ ] `## Strategy` has 9 paragraph-length decisions including the
  brain-category-detection-only paragraph that restates the three-state
  vocabulary and routes to `/aide:brain config` skill. Most are
  category-by-category enumerations.
  Traces to: `## Strategy` | Brevity Contract caps
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity

- [ ] `## Good examples` reproduces exact agent-dialog blocks verbatim with
  exact category names, exact file paths, and exact prose. Cap is 2-3
  brief; forbidden content.
  Traces to: `## Good examples` | Forbidden content
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Forbidden-content

- [ ] Sibling redundancy with the install service: the per-category-control
  pattern, the agent-driven-vs-tool-writes split, the prescription pattern,
  the malformed-JSON-aborts contract are all install-service-level invariants.
  Push to parent.
  Traces to: outcomes, Strategy | Sibling-redundancy
  Misalignment: spec-gap
  Category: Sibling-redundancy

## Retro

aide_upgrade's bloat is concentrated in category-name enumeration. The right
defense against drift between the registered MCP tool description and the
spec is a unit test asserting the description's accuracy against the
spec's category contract; spelling out all ten category names in three
different outcomes is forbidden enumeration.
